      "writtenOn": "2022-05-02T20:26:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that would actually decrease readability!  It would cause the same directory to be referred to as both \"legacy\" and \"non-legacy\" at the same time, which would be confusing.  I think it\u0027s a bit clearer the way I\u0027ve written it -- we have /data/system, which is the common stats directory, and within it we have both the legacy user stats directories and globalcomponentusage.  /data/system itself is no longer called a \"legacy\" directory, because it\u0027s not, and for that reason we don\u0027t delete it anymore.  Reading the diff is indeed a bit confusing, but I think that looking at just the new code, it makes more sense as-is.",
